# `golem/interest`

**Spatial interest management:** a `Grid` (spatial hash with configurable cell size, Insert/Remove/Move/Query) and a `Manager` that tracks per-session fields of interest. `FOI` describes a circular area anchored to an entity with a radius and hysteresis margin. `Diff` holds per-session enter/stay/exit entity ID lists computed each tick.

**`Manager`** owns the `Grid` and per-session known sets. Key methods: `AssignFOI(sessionID, entityID, radius, margin)` / `RemoveFOI(sessionID)` for lifecycle; `UpdateGrid(registry)` synchronises the grid with all live entities (inserts new, removes stale, moves changed) and records deleted globals in reused `removedGlobals`; `ComputeDiffs()` returns a `map[sessionID]*Diff` by querying each session's FOI against the grid, applying hysteresis (enter at `Radius`, exit at `Radius+Margin`), and diffing against the previous known set. `ComputeDiffsFiltered(allow)` applies an optional predicate before Entered/Stayed and forces Exited when a previously known entity becomes disallowed; `ComputeDiffs()` remains equivalent to a nil (allow-all) filter. Global entities (`IsGlobal() == true`) bypass spatial checks but still pass through the allow predicate (Server supplies visibility-group membership). Deleted globals emit Exited via `removedGlobals` even when the FOI anchor is not on the grid. This package does not store group policy.

**Not thread-safe.** All methods are called exclusively from the game tick goroutine (single-writer), under Server `interestMu`. The parent **`golem`** package creates and drives the Manager inside `runLoop`; consumers interact via `Server.AssignFOI` / `Server.RemoveFOI`.

Depends on **`golem/registry`** for the `Entity` interface and `Registry.All()`. Does **not** import `golem`, `golem/net`, `golem/visibility`, or `golem/world`.
